WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.268
Automaticity is the ability to perform practiced components with reduced conscious effort.

00:00:04.268 --> 00:00:07.394
It matters because attention and working memory are limited.

00:00:07.394 --> 00:00:10.172
When basic elements of a skill become fluent,

00:00:10.172 --> 00:00:14.340
the expert has more attention available for higher-level judgment, adaptation, and monitoring.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:19.550
A skilled performer does not have to think through every tiny step with equal effort,

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:21.981
which creates room for more complex decisions.

00:00:21.981 --> 00:00:25.454
Fluency can be powerful, but it can also be misleading.

00:00:25.454 --> 00:00:28.927
When performance feels easy, people may assume it is correct.

00:00:28.927 --> 00:00:31.359
Ease is not the same as accuracy.

00:00:31.359 --> 00:00:35.526
An expert may move quickly because the situation fits a well-learned pattern,

00:00:35.526 --> 00:00:39.694
but that same speed can become risky if the environment changes or

00:00:39.694 --> 00:00:41.778
if an important exception is hidden.

00:00:41.778 --> 00:00:44.209
Automaticity should support judgment, not replace it.

00:00:44.209 --> 00:00:46.293
Cognitive load still matters for experts.

00:00:46.293 --> 00:00:49.419
High-risk work often includes interruptions, fatigue, ambiguity, time pressure,

00:00:49.419 --> 00:00:50.461
and competing goals.

00:00:50.461 --> 00:00:56.018
Even skilled people can miss routine steps when memory is overloaded or the environment is noisy.

00:00:56.018 --> 00:00:59.839
That is why experts still use checklists, procedures, safeguards, peer review,

00:00:59.839 --> 00:01:00.880
and well-designed tools.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:05.396
These supports do not insult expertise; they protect it from predictable human limits.

00:01:05.396 --> 00:01:10.258
The practical lesson is to automate the right things while keeping critical thinking engaged.

00:01:10.258 --> 00:01:14.773
Routine components should become efficient enough that they do not consume all attention.

00:01:14.773 --> 00:01:18.941
At the same time, the system should create pauses for verification, escalation,

00:01:18.941 --> 00:01:23.109
and review when the stakes are high or the pattern is uncertain.

00:01:23.109 --> 00:01:25.540
Mature expertise combines fluency with disciplined safeguards.
